<title>TURKEY: Turkish Petkim H1 net profit falls.</title>
<headline>Turkish Petkim H1 net profit falls.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jan-June 1997 final</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>				  H1 1997	 H1 1996</p>
<p>				  -------	 -------</p>
<p>    Per share profit     3,613.02  vs   3,730.73</p>
<p>    Net Profit	    10,839.07  vs  11,192.20</p>
<p>    Net sales	     53,990.30  vs  29,924.89</p>
<p>    Operating profit     9,221.30  vs   7,328.10</p>
<p>    Exceptional income  14,536.80  vs  15,683.85</p>
<p>    Interest paid	    252.23  vs     299.67</p>
<p>    Total debts	   24,906.94  vs  21,080.81</p>
<p>    Equity		 112,330.66  vs  70,563.12</p>
<p>    Capital		  3,000.00  vs   3,000.00</p>
<p>NOTE - Largely state owned Petkim Petrokimya Holding A.S., Turkey's biggest petrochemical producer, is slated for partial sell-off, with 96 percent of its shares held by the privatisation administration OIB.</p>
<p>The figures above do not take into account Turkey's 78 percent consumer price inflation in June.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul Newsroom +90-212 275 08 75</p>
</text>
